;THE ACTIVE SITE OF THE FLAVOPROTEIN SUBUNIT CONTAINS A
CATALYTICALLY IMPORTANT DISULFIDE BRIDGE LOCATED ABOVE THE
PYRIMIDINE PORTION OF THE FLAVIN RING.  ANY OF A
TRYPTOPHAN, THREONINE OR TYROSINE SIDE CHAIN MAY PROVIDE A
PARTIAL CONDUIT FOR ELECTRON TRANSFER TO ONE OF THE HEME
GROUPS LOCATED 9.9 A FROM THE FLAVIN.
